WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.923
With a TMS, engineers
extract strings,

2
00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:06.500
send them out, and
wire translations back.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.135
It coordinates people well,

4
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:10.703
with translation memory,

5
00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:13.627
glossaries, review, and linguists.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.412
General Translation translates
your content in code and ships

7
00:00:17.412 --> 00:00:18.642
it with each release.

8
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.066
Keep the copy in your components,

9
00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:25.025
inside a T component from
its open-source libraries.

10
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.786
Add Korean to your config file,

11
00:00:27.786 --> 00:00:30.560
and the next build
translates the whole project.

12
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.852
Then npx gt translate or a
Locadex pull request translates

13
00:00:35.852 --> 00:00:36.850
each change.

14
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.226
Your team now ships
Korean with each release.
